From: "electron-claude[bot]"
 <279139701+electron-claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:16:13 +0000
Subject: build: guard the OpenXR browser tests in xr_browser_tests_vr_required
 on enable_openxr

https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8668230 extended
the Windows-only block of OpenXR browser tests in xr_browser_tests_vr_required
to Linux. That block depends on //device/vr:openxr_data, which is only defined
when enable_openxr is true. On Windows enable_vr implies enable_openxr, but on
Linux enable_vr is true even when checkout_openxr is false, so `gn gen` now
fails with an unresolved dependency when OpenXR is not checked out:

  //chrome/browser/vr:xr_browser_tests_vr_required needs //device/vr:openxr_data

Electron does not check out OpenXR, so guard the block on enable_openxr, which
restores the pre-existing (is_win implies enable_openxr) semantics.

This should be upstreamed.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/vr/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/vr/BUILD.gn
index 99256a7c0c2fda84f2a7b81c325831c4063a5114..37960063c529b12f87b71bf19a649de80523a3b0 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/vr/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/vr/BUILD.gn
@@ -539,8 +539,11 @@ if (enable_vr) {
 
       data_deps = []
 
-      # Windows and Linux tests and dependencies.
-      if (is_win || is_linux) {
+      # Windows and Linux tests and dependencies. These are OpenXR tests and
+      # depend on //device/vr:openxr_data, which only exists when
+      # enable_openxr is set, so guard them on it: on Linux, enable_vr can be
+      # true while enable_openxr is false (checkout_openxr = false).
+      if (enable_openxr && (is_win || is_linux)) {
         # Infrastructure.
         sources += [
           "test/ui_utils.cc",
